WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.960
The movie "Renfield" asks what Dracula's&nbsp;
relationship with his familiar Renfield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:08.340
might look like in the twenty-first century. Well,&nbsp;
there'd be a lot of therapy and even more blood.

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:11.700
"Renfield" is usually a propulsive and loud movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:11.700 --> 00:00:16.380
but for one moment before its big finale, there&nbsp;
is calm. Renfield and police officer Rebecca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.380 --> 00:00:20.100
Quincy recover in a small café after a&nbsp;
grisly battle at an apartment complex.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:22.740
"You know when something crazy&nbsp;
happens, and someone's like,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.480
'It's okay, I've seen way worse'? Everything&nbsp;
I saw you do today is gonna be my way worse."

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.120
It's there that Renfield comes clean about leaving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.720
his wife and child behind to serve as&nbsp;
Dracula's familiar. But the moment is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.720 --> 00:00:37.740
short lived. The duo quickly learns that&nbsp;
Count Dracula has a powerful new ally:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:37.740 --> 00:00:42.720
the Lobo crime family. Not only that, but these&nbsp;
gangsters have taken Quincy's sister hostage.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.100
This development ensures Quincy and Renfield&nbsp;
both have high stakes during the climax of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:50.820
movie. Renfield is, as ever, impressed with&nbsp;
Quincy's willingness to charge into battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:54.660
against their enemies. Seeing Renfield's&nbsp;
admiration, Quincy reminds him that anyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:58.500
can stand up to bullies and abusive people.&nbsp;
It's at this point that Renfield decides to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:02.880
help her battle the combined power of Dracula&nbsp;
and the mob. But they can't rush into battle&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.840
empty-handed. This is where Renfield's&nbsp;
decades of experience fighting Dracula's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:11.220
enemies becomes invaluable. He knows the best&nbsp;
weapons to use when you need to kill a vampire.

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.260
As the unforgettable opening chords of My&nbsp;
Chemical Romance's "Na Na Na" kick in one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:21.480
thing becomes very apparent: it's time for an&nbsp;
energetic montage. Renfield and Quincy start&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.080
to gather all the tools they need to fight&nbsp;
Dracula and his minions. As they scramble&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:29.400
across New Orleans looking for crucifixes and&nbsp;
anything else associated with killing vampires,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.400 --> 00:01:33.420
their determination to finally take out this&nbsp;
blood-sucking creep grows ever higher. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.420 --> 00:01:37.680
the most important part of the duo's&nbsp;
arsenal is…bugs. Since Renfield gets&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:40.800
his supernatural powers from chomping&nbsp;
on insects, it's time to go to every&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:45.000
bait-and-tackle store he can find and buy as&nbsp;
many tiny critters as possible to consume.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.540
This mission results in a gross-out&nbsp;
comedy moment where Renfield gobbles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:51.780
down a horde of insects loudly in the&nbsp;
passenger seat of Quincy's vehicle,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.780 --> 00:01:55.260
completely grossing her out in the&nbsp;
process. It's not a pretty sight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.260 --> 00:02:00.300
but it's a necessary one. Once Renfield is&nbsp;
powered up, he's ready to confront danger head-on.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.700
As the finale begins, Renfield easily takes&nbsp;
down random goons with his powers. But it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:09.780
when he finally encounters Teddy Lobo&nbsp;
that the real battle begins. Dracula&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:09.780 --> 00:02:13.260
has chosen him as his new familiar, and&nbsp;
as a result, has been given supernatural&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.260 --> 00:02:17.700
powers just like Renfield. This discovery&nbsp;
changes the nature of the battle. Renfield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.700 --> 00:02:20.940
has to use everything he's got to fight&nbsp;
the new and improved version of himself.

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:26.040
During their skirmish, Lobo constantly taunts&nbsp;
his rival, including emphasizing how he's "the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:31.020
yin" to Renfield's "yang." As Lobo viciously&nbsp;
attacks, Renfield shouts, "We've barely met&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:35.760
twice!" It calls out how little the two know about&nbsp;
each other and how ridiculous Lobo's claim is.

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.840
The battle between the two familiars rages&nbsp;
for a while before Renfield finally gains&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.380
the upper hand. In the final moments of&nbsp;
the battle, Dracula's original servant&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.380 --> 00:02:47.760
takes out Lobo in the most over-the-top way&nbsp;
possible. He kicks the mobster so hard in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.780
the stomach that he spews out fluids from&nbsp;
both his mouth and his rear before dying.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:56.580
While Renfield is off fighting Teddy Lobo,&nbsp;
Quincy makes her way to the office of Ella Lobo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.580 --> 00:03:00.360
where she hopes to find her sister. When she&nbsp;
arrives, Ella greets the police officer then&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:05.220
vanishes and the windows to the office are sealed&nbsp;
shut. With every window closed, sunlight can't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:05.220 --> 00:03:09.960
enter the room and harm the dark figure creeping&nbsp;
up behind her: Dracula. Decked out in a fabulous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:09.960 --> 00:03:14.760
red-colored cloak, Dracula doesn't go for the&nbsp;
jugular. Instead, he decides to make Rebecca&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.760 --> 00:03:19.200
an offer. Her sister is dying from incredibly&nbsp;
vicious wounds and the medicine of mortal men&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.580
can't save her. The blood of Dracula, which&nbsp;
can heal any wound, is her sister's only hope.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.580 --> 00:03:28.740
It's a particularly tense moment as the sisters&nbsp;
lost their father to Lobo earlier in the movie.

00:03:28.740 --> 00:03:34.140
Renfield bursts into the room as Quincy moves&nbsp;
closer to Dracula's embrace. Renfield begs her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.140 --> 00:03:36.960
not to give in to the dark lord, but&nbsp;
she says that she doesn't care about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.980
the consequences of being Dracula's servant.&nbsp;
She can't lose another member of her family.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.980 --> 00:03:46.020
Quincy finally hugs Dracula closely, but&nbsp;
the whole moment is a stunt. Her real goal&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:50.040
is to get close enough to the vampire to&nbsp;
activate the shutters and open the windows.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:54.360
Unfortunately for Quincy, her immediate&nbsp;
betrayal of Dracula doesn't go as planned.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:59.280
As she mashes the button to open the windows,&nbsp;
nothing happens. Her desperation rises as she&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:02.760
continues to mash the controller. Things&nbsp;
look grim for the cop until finally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:07.620
after several more presses, the windows finally&nbsp;
cooperate and open, bathing Dracula in sunlight.

00:04:07.620 --> 00:04:12.840
As the light pours in, Dracula howls in pain&nbsp;
and catches fire. He escapes by turning into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:18.600
a pack of bats, though now they're in flames. As&nbsp;
he flees, the Dracula bats crash into Ella Lobo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:21.900
still in the hallway, and knock her&nbsp;
out cold. Renfield and Quincy chase&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.900 --> 00:04:24.840
after the dark lord and track him to&nbsp;
a torture chamber in the Lobo family&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:28.680
compound. The battle between the three&nbsp;
of them continues in the foreboding room.

00:04:29.220 --> 00:04:33.420
Though badly burned by the sunlight, Dracula's&nbsp;
far from defeated. He's still an incredibly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:38.100
intimidating figure. At one point he levitates&nbsp;
into the air and grabs Quincy by the neck. With&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.100 --> 00:04:42.000
Renfield collapsed on the ground, succumbing&nbsp;
to his wounds, this is the moment where all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.560
hope looks lost. Fortunately for Quincy, her&nbsp;
arms are free enough to stab Dracula in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:50.520
foot. It's a move that the vicious vampire&nbsp;
initially laughs off as being a foolhardy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.520 --> 00:04:54.780
attempt to save her life. However, this maneuver&nbsp;
wasn't meant to kill Dracula or free herself.

00:04:54.780 --> 00:04:58.200
Instead, it was meant to force some&nbsp;
blood out of Dracula's injured foot,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:03.180
so it can drop onto Renfield and heal Dracula's&nbsp;
old familiar. The plan works like a charm, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.180 --> 00:05:07.560
the mystical blood reviving Renfield, who promptly&nbsp;
saves Quincy from the clutches of Dracula.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:11.220
It's time for the final confrontation.&nbsp;
Over the course of the movie, Renfield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.220 --> 00:05:14.100
has grown as an individual through&nbsp;
his work in the support meetings.

00:05:14.100 --> 00:05:15.540
"Sorry to interrupt."

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:16.560
"Are you okay?"

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:19.920
"I need to get out of a toxic relationship."

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.760
The most important lesson he learned at&nbsp;
the meetings is that victims in toxic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:27.540
relationships are the ones with all of&nbsp;
the power. He violently hammers this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.540 --> 00:05:31.800
point home to Dracula. While he's pummeling&nbsp;
his former boss, Quincy proceeds to trap the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:35.160
vampire in a spiritual containment field.&nbsp;
She learned the spell through some kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.600
of weird "wiccan Tumblr." After the dust and&nbsp;
blood settle, Renfield has finally taken his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:43.560
power back from Dracula and stopped the evil&nbsp;
creature of the night dead in his tracks.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:49.320
It's not enough to keep Dracula suspended in a&nbsp;
circle though, magical or otherwise. Renfield&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.320 --> 00:05:53.700
and Quincy have to completely destroy the beast.&nbsp;
Luckily, the final battle took them to a torture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:57.600
chamber filled with weapons. Renfield and&nbsp;
Quincy go to town dismembering, burning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:02.100
and torturing the vampire in every way imaginable.&nbsp;
Renfield's recurring narration throughout the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:02.100 --> 00:06:06.000
movie pops in again to remark to the audience&nbsp;
that neither he nor his partner is sure what&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:10.140
can actually kill Dracula, so they try to just&nbsp;
throw everything at the wall and see what sticks.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.560
Going this route inspires some of the&nbsp;
more amusingly heightened gags in all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.880
of "Renfield." The inexplicable presence of&nbsp;
items like a cement mixer and an ice cube tray&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:23.040
as ways of brutally killing Dracula are amusing&nbsp;
sight gags. This is especially true since these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:27.540
cartoonish vampire-killing "weapons" are far&nbsp;
from common in the pantheon of vampire movies.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:31.560
Eventually, the barrage of sight gags and&nbsp;
creative murders gives way to Renfield and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:31.560 --> 00:06:35.160
Quincy dropping a bunch of chopped-up&nbsp;
cubes of Dracula's corpse into a pit.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:39.600
Renfield notes in the narration that he's far&nbsp;
from certain that this will kill off Dracula&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:43.560
forever. But he knows that at the very&nbsp;
least, the dark lord won't heal easily.

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:49.200
With Dracula defeated, it's time to take care of&nbsp;
one last Villain. Renfield and Quincy return to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:54.060
the scene of their final confrontation with Ella&nbsp;
Lobo. Still incapacitated from Dracula's flight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.060 --> 00:06:58.320
Quincy manages to cuff the mobster and send her&nbsp;
off to prison. Quincy finally rescues her sister,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.320 --> 00:07:02.520
who has been brought back to life with Dracula's&nbsp;
blood. The pair reconcile their differences,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.520 --> 00:07:06.900
share a hug, and then Quincy heads over to&nbsp;
regroup with Renfield. Now free of his master,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:11.040
the former familiar has understandably&nbsp;
complicated emotions swirling around inside him.

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:14.400
Though he still doubts that he's much&nbsp;
better than Dracula, Quincy reassures&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.400 --> 00:07:18.420
Renfield that he's given something important&nbsp;
to the world. When he asks what that is,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:23.220
Quincy says that he's shown that it's never too&nbsp;
late for someone to be a hero. It's an exchange&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.220 --> 00:07:27.540
that closes out Renfield's character arc and&nbsp;
lays the core theme of the entire film bare.

00:07:27.540 --> 00:07:31.740
Life begins to calm down after&nbsp;
Dracula's defeat. As the movie closes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.740 --> 00:07:34.020
we discover that Renfield's&nbsp;
narration has all occurred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.020 --> 00:07:36.780
while speaking to his support group&nbsp;
for victims of abusive relationships.

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:39.600
"But if you were to stop focusing&nbsp;
on his needs, what would happen?"

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:42.180
"He won't grow to full power."

00:07:42.180 --> 00:07:44.820
"Exactly! He won't grow to full power!"

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:47.880
However, in a twist perfectly&nbsp;
suited to Renfield's world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:51.960
the members of the group are all the resurrected&nbsp;
victims of Dracula's attack from earlier in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.960 --> 00:07:55.860
the movie. Renfield has brought them back&nbsp;
from the dead using the dark lord's blood.

00:07:55.860 --> 00:08:00.660
Though it might be a little convenient to bring&nbsp;
back all of these characters so easily, it's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:05.760
fitting end for a film that relishes in silliness&nbsp;
and over-the-top antics. The camera even lingers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:10.560
on a jug of blood situated next to cookies and&nbsp;
napkins for the final shot of the entire feature.

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:14.880
Viewers expecting "Renfield" to conclude&nbsp;
with teases for further adventures involving&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:14.880 --> 00:08:19.140
Nicolas Cage's Dracula will leave the film&nbsp;
sorely disappointed. Despite Renfield not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:19.140 --> 00:08:22.620
being sure that he and Quincy have truly&nbsp;
destroyed Dracula, the movie ends on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:28.140
definitively standalone note. There are no hints&nbsp;
for potential sequels or even an after-the-credits&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:28.140 --> 00:08:31.860
scene. It's clear that "Renfield" is&nbsp;
meant to function as a one-off story.

00:08:31.860 --> 00:08:36.180
Fans can still hope though. The chemistry&nbsp;
between Nicolas Cage and Nicholas Hoult&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:40.242
is the absolute standout of the film, and it&nbsp;
would be a shame to not revisit their dynamic.

00:08:40.242 --> 00:08:43.020
"Hello, Renfield, marvelous attire."

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.180
And Awkwafina as always delivers a hilarious&nbsp;
counterpoint to the violent existence of her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:52.380
superpowered partner. Seeing how Renfield&nbsp;
matures with his new knowledge of overcoming&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.380 --> 00:08:56.460
toxic relationships could be a great starting&nbsp;
point for a sequel. And it would be hilarious&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.460 --> 00:09:01.080
to watch how he brings his emotional maturity with&nbsp;
him to battle creatures of the night. Only time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.080 --> 00:09:04.200
success, and maybe a little bit&nbsp;
of Dracula's blood will tell.

